$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure C for the cross-coupling
reaction of phosphate 5 with boronic acids or NPG boronates. Toluene (4
mL/mmol) and aq. potassium phosphate (2M, 1.3 -2.0 mL/mmol) was added to
a mixture of enolphosphate 6 (1 eq.), Pd(OAc)2 (0.01 -0.04 eq, 1 -4 mol
%), RuPhos (0.017 -0.068 eq., 1.7 -6.8 %), and boronic acid or boronate
(1.3 -2.0 eq.). The resultant mixture was stirred at 50 °C. Then the
mixture was diluted with diethylether and organic layer was washed with
1M KOH and brine, dried over magnesium sulphate and concentrated under
reduce pressure. Formed product was isolated by column chromatography.
(Z)-(1-Phenyl-1-(4-methoxyphenyl)hexen-2-yl)(diethyl) phosphate (Z)-6a.
The title compound was prepared according the general procedure C
starting from (Z)-3b (1.950 g, 5 mmol), 4-methoxyphenylboronic acid
(0.988 g, 6.5 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.011 g, 1 mol %), RuPhos (0.040 g, 1.7
mol %), 2M aq. K3PO4 (6.5 mL), and toluene (20 mL). The reaction mixture
was stirred 20 h at 50 °C, following column chromatography (silica gel,
EtOAc-hexane 1:2, UV detection).
(Z)-(Diethyl)(1-(4-methylphenyl)-2-(4-fluorophenyl)-2-(4-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl)
phosphate (Z)-6b. The title compound was prepared according the general
procedure C starting from (Z)-5d (1.360 g, 3 mmol), 4-fluorophenylboronic
acid (0.546 g, 3.9 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (0.007 g, 1 mol %), RuPhos (0.024 g,
1.7 mol %), 2M aq. K3PO4 (3.9 mL), and toluene (12 mL). The reaction
mixture was stirred 20 h at 50 °C, following column chromatography
(silica gel, EtOAc-hexane 1:2, UV detection). 1.270 g (90%) of the title
compound product as a yellowish glass. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.07
(dt, J = 7.1 Hz, J (P-H) = 1.2 Hz, 6H), 2.29 (s, 3H), 3.56-80 (m, 4H)
overlapping with 3.71 (s, 3H), 6.62 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 2H), 6.87 (d, J = 8.7
Hz, 2H), 6.98-7.08 (m, 4H), 7.26 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H) overlapping with
CHCl3, 7.43 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (75.5 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 15.75 (d, J (C-P) =
7.2 Hz), 21.27, 54.99, 63.76 (d, J (C-P) = 6.0 Hz), 113.28, 114.76 (d, J
(C-F) = 21.5 Hz), 128.30 (d, J (C-P) = 8.3 Hz), 128.48, 130.15, 131.68
overlapping with 131.75, 132.11, 132.26, 135.94, 138.19, 143.48 (d, J
(C-P) = 8.5 Hz), 158.70, 161.82 (d, J (C-F) = 246 Hz). 19F NMR (CDCl3):
-115.74. HRMS (ESI): Calc. for C26H28FO5P+Na+ [M+Na+] = 493.1550; Found:
493.1550. Rf = 0.3.
