$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-Methyl-4-acetamido-indan (27). Compound 26 (4 mmol) was dissolved in
dioxan (10 mL), the mixture was degassed and placed under an argon
atmosphere. Pd(PPh3)4 (10%mol) and 5 mL of degassed 2 N Na2CO3 were
added. Ttrimethylboroxine (1.5 eq.) was then added to the mixture via a
syringe and the whole was heated at reflux for 10 h. After cooling, the
reaction mixture was diluted with 5 mL of water and filtered. The mixture
was extracted with dichloromethane, the organic phase was dried over
anhydrous Na2SO4, and the solvent distilled off under reduced pressure.
The product was purified by flash chromatography (AcOEt-hexane; 3-7).
Compound 27 in 80% yield as a white solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.57 (d, 1H,
Har, J= 8.2); 6.96 (d, 1H, Har, J= 8); 6.89 (br s, 1H, NH); 2.86 (t, 2H,
CH2, J= 7.4); 2.82 (t, 2H, CH2, J= 7.4); 2.22 (s, 3H, CH3(ar)); 2.17 (s,
3H, CH3); 2.10 (qn, 2H, CH2, J= 7.5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
